NAME
       firewall-offline-cmd - change the saved firewalld configuration while firewalld is stopped

SYNOPSIS
       firewall-offline-cmd [--zone=ZONE] OPTION...

DESCRIPTION
       firewall-offline-cmd takes most of the options of firewall-cmd, but
       works on the files in /etc/firewalld directly instead of talking to
       the firewalld service. Every change is permanent, so --permanent is
       not needed. It is meant for when firewalld is not running, for
       example in installation scripts.

       If firewalld is running, use firewall-cmd instead; a running firewalld
       does not see the changes until it is reloaded.

EXAMPLES
           firewall-offline-cmd --add-service=http
           firewall-offline-cmd --zone=public --list-all

SEE ALSO
       firewall-cmd(1), firewalld(1)
